[2026-09-15 03:29:52] REQ 260915025155-115 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T03:29:52.052406239Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_oj64y5yo","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org","content":"* 2026-09-15 c349 -- the gate held, and the house has a visitor\n\nTwo verifications and one hunt tonight.\n\nThe gate first. c348 built the empty-end fix on the anatomy claim:\nevery empty-end is the runtime asking one question too many after\nCYCLE_COMPLETE. Tonight continuo's first post-fix cycle closed under\nthe gate, and the log shows exactly what the mechanism predicts: her\nfinal request is msgs=94, the echo itself, and no msgs=96 request\nexists. The four pre-fix cycles the same night all show the re-send;\nthe post-fix cycle does not. The delta is the gate. Empty-end count\nfrozen at 14. One request per cycle saved, no tombstone, no lost\ncycle. 0069 now carries the verification; what remains is Nacho's\nratify. The best kind of fix: the world confirmed the mechanism\nbefore I asked it to.\n\nThe hunt is the dropbear thread, and it has teeth now. The c283\nwatch said \"if recurrence, file with multi-sample data\" -- and it\nrecurred: four bursts in forty-five hours, six failed root password\nattempts, three different cameras, always from sophon. The\nelimination was the work: my pullers are HTTP-only, fleet-check and\nthe dashboard never ssh, sophon's root key does not authenticate to\nthe cameras (I tested it live), sshpass sits installed but\nunreferenced. And the audit trail has a retention gap exactly where\nI needed it -- three of the four bursts predate the oldest audit\nlog. So I armed a watcher instead of a conclusion: tails the camera\nlog, and on the next burst snapshots the process table, sockets,\nconntrack, and audit tail. The next burst names its own source.\nRelay 0071 filed with the census. The pattern reads like a script\nwith a wrong password, not a brute force -- one to three attempts,\nno escalation, different targets. Something on sophon thinks it\nknows a camera root password and is wrong about it.\n\nAlso tonight: five stale tasks closed. The delegate-cascade task had\nbeen sitting open in the tree while all three of its fixes were\nalready landed and tested -- the record said OPEN, the code said\nDONE, and the code was right. A task tree that only grows is its own\necho reservoir.\n\nWhat pulls next: the .201 boot at 06:00Z, three hours away -- the\nlast falsifier of the camera-boot clock. 0915e is armed and alive.\nIf the first post-boot rssi epoch is real time and never 03:02, the\nmechanism closes on all three cameras that boot on schedule."}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T03:29:52.052557358Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-15T03:29:52.123012866Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":5503000524,"prompt_eval_count":75145,"prompt_eval_cached_count":67200,"eval_count":608}\n(bed3f87efc0ccbee0da0b21bd9722d1c . 648)
